## Task Dependency Mapping (V8)

> Gates map to Claude Code 2026 Tasks system for automated dependency enforcement.

### Gate → Task Mapping

Gates translate to Task dependencies:
- **Gate criteria** → Individual tasks with `TaskCreate`
- **Gate unlock** → `TaskUpdate(addBlocks=[...])`
- **Gate block** → `TaskUpdate(addBlockedBy=[...])`

| Gate | Blocking Tasks | Unlocked Tasks | Task IDs |
|------|----------------|----------------|----------|
| Gate ${GATE_NUMBER} | Sprint ${BLOCKING_SPRINT} all tasks | Sprint ${UNLOCKED_SPRINT} all tasks | gate-${GATE_NUMBER}-* |

### Creating Gate Tasks

```bash
# Gate criteria as individual tasks
TaskCreate(subject="Gate ${GATE_NUMBER}: ${CRITERION_1}", description="...")
TaskCreate(subject="Gate ${GATE_NUMBER}: ${CRITERION_2}", description="...")

# Gate pass task (blocked by all criteria)
TaskCreate(subject="Gate ${GATE_NUMBER} Pass", description="All criteria met")
TaskUpdate(taskId="gate-${GATE_NUMBER}-pass", addBlockedBy=["gate-${GATE_NUMBER}-1", "gate-${GATE_NUMBER}-2"])

# Unlock downstream sprints when gate passes
TaskUpdate(taskId="sprint-${UNLOCKED_SPRINT}-01", addBlockedBy=["gate-${GATE_NUMBER}-pass"])
```

### Gate Status via TaskList

Instead of manual status tracking, query Tasks:
```bash
TaskList  # Shows gate tasks with status (pending/in_progress/completed)
TaskGet(taskId="gate-${GATE_NUMBER}-pass")  # Check if gate passed
```

### Auto-Unblock Pattern

When gate passes, downstream sprints auto-unblock:
```
Gate ${GATE_NUMBER} criteria tasks (all complete)
    └── Gate ${GATE_NUMBER} Pass (completes)
        └── Sprint ${UNLOCKED_SPRINT} tasks (unblocked)
```

